ple/bill-brown"}, {"title": "humanitiesday2014.uchicago.edu", "url": "https://humanitiesday2014.uchicago.edu/node/356.html"}, {"title": "Tripti Joshi (Editor)", "url": "https://alchetron.com/Bill-Brown-(critical-theory)"}]}, "The search confirmed Bill Brown's Ph.D. and his title, but found nothing on a B.A. or graduation year.\n\n- **Ph.D.:** The University of Chicago faculty page lists Ph.D., Stanford University, 1989.\n- **Title:** He is the Karla Scherer Distinguished Service Professor in American Culture at Chicago, appointed in the department of English language and literature, the department of visual arts, and the college.\n- **Thing theory:** Brown is the figure most associated with the theory. He edited a special issue of Critical Inquiry on it in 2001 and published a monograph on the subject entitled A Sense of Things. His 2015 book is *Other Things*, per one of the university's event pages.\n- **B.A.:** None of the results name his undergraduate institution or degree year. One mirror site (Alchetron) lists \"Duke University\" under education, but it is a copy of a Wikipedia-style entry and I could not verify it, so treat it as unconfirmed."], "durationSeconds": 5.1388015419999995, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01SWPSVdczRnbVpuq6BENikU", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
